# build outputs
build/
out/
*.obj
*.o
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

# editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.vs/
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# local scratch
scratch/

# ImGui layout files — per-user, per-host, and deliberately NOT tracked: a
# committed one hid the fact that docking had never engaged (2026-08-06), by
# giving every run a layout that looked plausible. Untracked keeps "first run
# on a clean machine" an honest test. Delete yours to re-seed the default.
imgui*.ini

# ── WHAT THE PRE-PUBLISH PROBE CAUGHT (2026-09-01) ──────────────────────────
#
# A dry-run `git add -An` into a throwaway git-dir is the only honest way to
# read a .gitignore. Two things it staged that must never be published:

# CTest's scratch directory. `ctest` run from the repo root (rather than from
# build/) writes Testing/Temporary/LastTest.log into the SOURCE tree, and that
# log carries absolute paths under the builder's home directory.
Testing/

# Agent config: personal, not project. `.claude/settings.json` here is this
# machine's permission allowlist — 108 lines of one-off invocations and
# absolute paths under the author's home. It tells a stranger nothing about
# Void Maiz and everything about one laptop. If a curated, path-free config is
# ever worth sharing it can be added deliberately with `git add -f`.
.claude/

# Alternate build trees (build2/, build3/, …) alongside the canonical build/.
build*/
